      "before": " The original finite-support argument\nalso covers modifications where that normal-degree test alone\nwould give no information.",
      "after": "",
      "reason": "Delete the repeated scope comparison at the end of the normal-degree step. The initial statement already gives the finite-modification assertion and the nonzero-normal-degree assertion with their exact hypotheses. The full finite-image/equivariance/orbit proof in steps1–3 and the derivative/Abel–Jacobi normal-line proof in step4 remain. The removed sentence adds no map, formula or case definition; no new comparison of the two methods is asserted.",
      "source_sha256": "3542f2632cad8f1eb78f0f30f8a64ca91998f3bd1d97010ca76d89297c4bffe7",
      "pdf_sha256": "702aaa0abd1a4d8376e213ecaf03a0296592e22063f26db324d805502987e66e",
      "candidate18_synctex_pages": [
        214
      ],
      "retained_witnesses": [
        {
          "exact_text": "Suppose $p:Y\\to H$ is a finite composition of point blow-ups,\nallowing infinitely near centres, and at least one point of $E$\nis an image of its exceptional locus.",
          "sha256": "ff71cb6340fd50f0d71d79090c6bba8b864b7cd39f45c27500f5e21083483a5a",
          "source_line": 22222,
          "preserved_byte_identically": true
        },
        {
          "exact_text": "More generally, if a compact smooth surface contains a preserved\nmarked elliptic curve $E$ of nonzero normal degree $d$, every\nholomorphic automorphism restricting to translation by $b$ on $E$\nmust satisfy $d\\,b=0$ in $E$.",
          "sha256": "51d8350c2f2f2a568b7158b2d15e26ca3e4e086b2340efafa081d1bde72d6511",
          "source_line": 22232,
          "preserved_byte_identically": true
        },
        {
          "exact_text": "Thus preservation of $N$ forces $d b=0$.",
          "sha256": "61c1262819617e7779ebb84b0a76252e23b7f0deb13f4bf26ad84248257c4d2e",
          "source_line": 22294,
          "preserved_byte_identically": true
